+
+### Out-of-Core Voxelization with Appearance Data
+An extension of the out-of-core SVO construction that handles appearance data (colors, normals, texture coordinates) by interpolating vertex attributes during voxelization and propagating them to higher levels of the octree, provided the data is available locally [S1].
+
+### Sparse-Voxel-Octree (SVO) Voxelization
+A variant of voxel cone tracing that uses a Sparse-Voxel-Octree (SVO) instead of a regular 3D texture to store lighting data, reducing GPU memory usage by dynamically instantiating nodes [S2, unofficial]. The voxelization procedure undergoes three rasterization passes, once for each spatial axis [S2, unofficial]. Storing lighting data in a sparse octree is significantly more challenging to implement and navigate compared to a regular grid [S2, unofficial].
 
